From 5fb5d26012ef16ba1f4c27611852ea6385d34663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:46:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/17] ASoC: apple: add S8000 (A9) MCA driver

CPU DAI for the A9 MCA ("mca-version 4"), following iOS 16.7.10's
AppleAE2MCA::_setIISConfig_v4: reset/flush with bounded polls, sample
size, TX FIFO watermark, slot masks, TX config and the frame register;
start sets TX enable then the frame run bit, stop resets TX.

The MCA's MCLK control word is exported as a clock (iOS writes 0x58,
nclk/2 with output enabled, for the codec's 12 MHz MCLK), and the
i2s-switch route is applied from DT while the port runs.

iOS moves samples with SmartIO DMA (endpoint 0x28). With "dmas" the
generic dmaengine PCM is used. Without it a timer-driven PCM keeps the
stream running so the clocks, codec and amplifiers can be tested, with
an experimental CPU-fed FIFO mode if a FIFO port is given in DT.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>
